            <ArticleTitle>Familial hypercholesterolaemia presenting with coronary artery disease in a young patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2013-008718</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2013008718</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A man in his early 20s presented with an angina on exertion and postprandial angina. Upon examination, the patient had carotid artery bruit and multiple tendon xanthomas. His lipid profile showed a very high total and low-density lipoprotein cholesterol; treadmill test was strongly positive. Subsequent coronary angiogram revealed triple vessel disease. The patient underwent revascularisation and is on lipid lowering therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
